Small Council
=============

Small Council (formerly Ultra Council) is a derivative work of **Carmack-Council**
by Sam Hudson, originally released under the MIT License.

    Original project : Carmack-Council
    Author           : Sam Hudson (github.com/SamJHudson01)
    Source           : https://github.com/SamJHudson01/Carmack-Council
    License          : MIT (see LICENSE)

What is derived and what is new
-------------------------------
Small Council keeps the named-expert council idea, the council-review,
council-plan, council-implement, spec-writer, and test-architect modes
(substantially rewritten), and several reference documents. It adds:

  - context-core      — a reusable context-engineering pipeline that every
                        mode runs on (the original had no shared pipeline);
  - council-init      — per-project tailoring of the roster, gates, and
                        codebase map;
  - council-research  — an evidence-graded investigation mode;
  - the council-worker and council-verifier agents and the SessionStart hook;
  - durable project memory, the codebase map, and the .council/ layout;
  - an evals harness (validation, structural, hook, and behavioral drills).

The seat reference documents under `references/` — `security.md`,
`refactoring.md`, and the `quality-*.md` set other than
`quality-performance.md` — and the spec-writer documents originate from
Carmack-Council and remain under its MIT license. Their copyright notice is
preserved in LICENSE as the MIT terms require.

Grateful acknowledgment to Sam Hudson for the original Carmack-Council.
